I should be candid about confidence: this panoramic image shows generalized severe horizontal bone loss, and the distinction between a true periapical radiolucency and the radiolucent crestal bone/overlying sinus is genuinely difficult at this resolution. The four regions above are the most convincing localized periapical radiolucencies I could identify — well-defined radiolucencies at the mandibular left canine/premolar apices (graded 4), a rounded lucency adjacent to the maxillary right molar apex (3), and a periapical lucency at the mandibular right premolar near the gold restoration (3). Other description-level features (paucity of clearly discrete lesions elsewhere) mean this list may under- or over-call individual teeth.
